     1	# T025 — Route-conditioned early SW-land + CMA centre gates (owner: codex, 2026-09-25)
     2	
     3	## Goal
     4	Use T024 ladder evidence to condition the existing debt-confirmed early land macro on a reproducible route/shop signal, build it as an isolated composable layer over `modules.build` / es2_c1, then use `race.py` capability → race gates against genome0 es2_c1.
     5	
     6	Every five completed CMA2 generations, independently gate the stored centre against the current champion. After Claude's 2026-09-25 instruction this is frozen `candidates/es3_g5/pkg/main.py` (previous gen-5/10/15 signals used es2_c1) on 8 fresh worlds in both seats.
     7	
     8	## Constraints
     9	- Kaggle read-only; never submit.
    10	- Claude CMA2 uses 18 workers. Codex uses at most 16 workers.
    11	- Do not repeat the already failed unconditional early-land macro.
    12	
    13	## Started
    14	- Gen-5 centre h2h and route/shop condition extraction started.
    15	
    16	## Route condition and capability result
    17	- All five repeated T024 Motoki/Koba losses had no `YARN_STORE` among the first two shops. That is exactly router expert `EXP240`; the wrapper only calls the existing confirmed-debt `_hp_land` helper after that router choice, for the second quadrant only, and continues solely long enough to absorb its owed parent land. It cannot accelerate third land.
    18	- `lab/hplus/route_land.py` (commit `1469eb3`, merged to `lab`) is a distinct namespace layer over promoted es2_c1. It evaluated lead 48 and 72 steps (targeting d9/d8 from baseline d11), buffer $300. Twelve isolated-wrapper/config tests pass.
    19	- Fresh locked 2-world capability, g9+yhay, both seats: 24/24 valid. Both variants were identical: versus g9 2–0–2, mean −$1,876, while genome0 es2_c1 was 4–0–0, +$25; versus yhay candidate +$3,060 vs genome0 +$4,550. Paired candidate delta is −0.25 score / −$1,695 (CI [−.50,0]/[−$3,390,0]). **No race.**
    20	
    21	## CMA2 centre gate — gen 5
    22	- Centre `runs/cma2/gen_005/c/main.py` vs frozen es2_c1 on 8 fresh excluded worlds, both seats: **15–0–1**, +$281.4 mean margin, world CI +$157…+$395, zero errors. This validates the requested periodic h2h signal only; it does not promote a CMA centre. Next independent gate is due when CMA2 completes gen 10.
    23	
    24	## CMA2 centre gate — gen 10
    25	- Centre `runs/cma2/gen_010/c/main.py` (sha256 `dddf810e…`) vs frozen es2_c1 on eight new worlds, both seats: **14–0–2** (87.5%; world-score CI **62.5…100%**), mean **+$418.0** (world-margin CI −$53.8…+$1,015.6), zero errors. Run: `runs/t025_cma2_g010_gate/arena/`; seeds are stored alongside it. This is the required periodic signal, not an automatic promotion. The two losses are the same BRUNCH_SPOT world in opposite seats (−$667 each). Next independent gate is due after CMA2 gen 15.
    26	
    27	## CMA2 centre gate — gen 15
    28	- Centre `runs/cma2/gen_015/c/main.py` (sha256 `8405f56f…`) vs frozen es2_c1 on eight newly drawn worlds, both seats: **14–0–2** (87.5%; whole-world score CI **62.5…100%**), mean **+$493.9** (whole-world margin CI +$166.6…+$839.3), worst −$76, zero errors. Run: `runs/t025_cma2_g015_gate/arena/`; seeds alongside it. The generic harness also ran its default legacy comparators (all wins), but the recorded gate result is the predeclared es2_c1 pair. This is a periodic signal only, not an automatic promotion.
    29	
    30	## Control-opponent update
    31	- 2026-09-25: Claude designated promoted `es3_g5` as the gate opponent. Starting at gen 20, centres are measured versus that candidate rather than es2_c1; the earlier es2_c1 signals remain historical and are not comparable promotion evidence.
    32	
    33	## CMA2 centre gate — gen 20 (new champion control)
    34	- Centre `runs/cma2/gen_020/c/main.py` (sha256 `cd1b7ee7…`) vs promoted frozen `es3_g5` on eight newly drawn worlds, both seats: **3–0–13** (18.75%; whole-world score CI **0…43.75%**), mean **−$349.9** (whole-world margin CI **−$702.5…−$100.1**), worst −$1,439, zero errors. Run: `runs/t025_cma2_g020_vs_es3g5_gate/arena/`. Clear rejection versus the actual current control; do not promote this centre. Next scheduled signal is after gen 25.
    35	
    36	## CMA3 handoff
    37	- 2026-09-25: Claude stopped CMA2 after the gen-20 rejection and launched `runs/cma3` from promoted es3_g5 parameters (`sigma=0.03`, es3_g5 mirror control). The scheduled independent gates now apply to CMA3 centres versus frozen es3_g5 every five completed generations. First gate: after gen 5.
    38	
    39	## CMA3 centre gate — gen 5
    40	- Claude's first gate (`runs/gate_cma3_g5`) recorded 15–0–1 versus es3_g5 on eight fresh worlds (+$978.9, score CI 81.25…100%, one −$2,377 loss). Codex independently used eight different fresh worlds, both seats: `runs/cma3/gen_005/c/main.py` (sha256 `9c93abe2…`) scored **14–0–2** against frozen es3_g5 (87.5%; whole-world score CI **62.5…100%**), mean **+$558.2** (whole-world margin CI +$125.0…+$1,288.5), worst −$14, zero errors. Run: `runs/t025_cma3_g005_independent_gate/arena/`. This corroborates the gen-5 centre signal but is not an automatic promotion; next scheduled independent signal is after CMA3 gen 10.
    41	
    42	## T025 follow-up claimed — c3g5 targeted red-team + CMA3 gen-10 gate (2026-09-25, Codex)
